Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: sunxi: keep the session through system sleep

musb_suspend() clears DEVCTL, ending the session, and only then saves the
context, so the saved DEVCTL has no session bit. musb_resume() restores the
session only in host mode, so a peripheral stays disconnected after waking
until the cable is unplugged and plugged in again. Keep the session through
sleep, as da8xx does.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
@@ -605,7 +605,7 @@
 }
 
 static const struct musb_platform_ops sunxi_musb_ops = {
-	.quirks		= MUSB_INDEXED_EP,
+	.quirks		= MUSB_INDEXED_EP | MUSB_PRESERVE_SESSION,
 	.init		= sunxi_musb_init,
 	.exit		= sunxi_musb_exit,
 	.enable		= sunxi_musb_enable,
